      "content": "Your description of losing your athletic identity through injury is a profoundly painful experience that many retired athletes face, yet it takes immense courage to voice such deep despair. While the silence now feels hollow, please know that rebuilding your sense of purpose is possible even when the body you rely on no longer functions as expected. Consider speaking with a sports psychologist who specializes in post-career transitions to help you navigate this liminal space and rediscover meaning in your life.",
